{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-17T09:31:55.819Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n**Task 1 — Autopilot configuration** (cli-foundation \"Autopilot values\").\n\n- Added `src/core/foundation/config-autopilot.ts` with the `AutopilotConfig` type and `validateAutopilotConfig`, following `config-auto-steer.ts`: keys checked first, then `enabled`, with the three error texts (`autopilot must be an object`, `autopilot.<key> is not supported`, `autopilot.enabled must be a boolean`).\n- Wired it through `OsqConfig`, `OsqUserConfig`, and `defineConfig`, adding the resolved block only when the user supplied one (so no config file → no `autopilot` key, and `DEFAULT_CONFIG` has none).\n- Added `tests/autopilot-config.test.ts` proving each table row through `defineConfig`.\n\n**Deviation:** the task's line-arithmetic for `config.ts` landed one counted line over the 250 cap on today's tree, so besides the described edits (autopilot destructured out, `validatedPlanner` collapsed, blank line removed) I inlined the resolver into its spread instead of keeping a `resolvedAutopilot` const. Final file: 249 `wc -l` / 250 counted lines, `biome check` clean.\n\n**Verification:** task verify green (7/7); `pnpm verify` passed end to end (typechecks, build, all tests, and lint — 1267 files checked, no fixes). Changed files are all inside scope; result written to `openspec/changes/200-autopilot-queue-run/.run/results/1.md`."}}
